# Tamiyo, Collector of Tales: "Spells and abilities your opponents control can't cause you to ... sacrifice permanents." Bot1's
# Goblin Welder targets Bot2's Mox Jet and the Black Lotus in Bot2's graveyard: as it resolves, Bot2 can't be made to sacrifice
# the Mox, so that part of the effect does nothing (Sigarda's ruling: "That part of the effect does nothing", CR 101.2) - the
# Mox stays, and the Lotus still returns to the battlefield under Bot2's control (CR 101.3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Goblin Welder
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Tamiyo, Collector of Tales
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Goblin Welder.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Tamiyo, Collector of Tales.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Welder.Activate
Bot1.Target(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Target(Black Lotus)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Jet; Tamiyo, Collector of Tales; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
